---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Sources from '~/components/common/Sources.astro';
import StructuredData from '~/components/common/StructuredData.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/common/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from 'astrowind:config';
import { authorRef, dateFields, organizationRef, siteUrl } from '~/utils/schema';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Editorial and Medical Review Policy',
  description:
    'How Quit Smoking Hub writes, sources and corrects smoking cessation pages, and why no page here claims clinical review, medical sign-off or a named doctor.',
};

const site = siteUrl(SITE.site);
const url = `${site}/editorial-policy/`;

const pageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Editorial and Medical Review Policy',
  headline: 'Editorial and Medical Review Policy',
  description: metadata.description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  isPartOf: { '@id': `${site}/#website` },
  author: authorRef(SITE.site),
  publisher: organizationRef(SITE.site),
  ...dateFields('2026-11-11', '2026-11-11'),
};

const pageSources = [
  {
    label: 'WHO — Clinical treatment guideline for tobacco cessation in adults (2024)',
    url: 'https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240096431',
  },
  {
    label: 'NICE — Tobacco: preventing uptake, promoting quitting and treating dependence (NG209)',
    url: 'https://www.nice.org.uk/guidance/ng209',
  },
  {
    label: 'USPSTF — Tobacco use in adults and pregnant women: counselling and interventions (2021)',
    url: 'https://www.uspreventiveservicestaskforce.org/uspstf/recommendation/tobacco-use-in-adults-and-pregnant-women-counseling-and-interventions',
  },
  {
    label: 'Cochrane — Nicotine replacement therapy for smoking cessation',
    url: 'https://www.cochranelibrary.com/cdsr/doi/10.1002/14651858.CD000146.pub4/full',
  },
  { label: 'CDC — Tobacco and smoking', url: 'https://www.cdc.gov/tobacco/index.html' },
  { label: 'NHS — Quit smoking', url: 'https://www.nhs.uk/better-health/quit-smoking/' },
];
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <StructuredData slot="head" schema={[pageSchema]} />
  <Breadcrumbs bar items={[{ text: 'Home', href: '/' }, { text: 'Editorial and Medical Review Policy' }]} />

  <section class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 pt-8 md:pt-12 pb-4">
    <p class="text-base font-bold tracking-wide uppercase text-secondary mb-2 text-center">Trust and transparency</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading text-center">
      Editorial and medical review policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-lg text-muted text-center">
      Who writes this site, where the evidence comes from, what we refuse to publish, and what our pages do not claim.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 space-y-10">
    <div class="card p-6 border-l-4 border-l-primary">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">The short version</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading dark:text-slate-200">No page on this site has been reviewed by a clinician.</strong>
          We do not have a named medical reviewer, and we do not describe any page as medically reviewed, medically
          approved, or clinically verified.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every evidence page names the public guidance and research it draws on, and states how strong that evidence
          is.
        </li>
        <li>
          We publish general education only. We do not give doses, injection instructions, prescriptions,
          individualised treatment plans, or promises that any method will work.
        </li>
        <li>Community experiences are labelled as community reports everywhere they appear. They are not evidence.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">1. Who produces this site</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        Quit Smoking Hub is produced by the SmokingCessationHub editorial team: a small group that researches, writes,
        structures and maintains the pages, and operates the de-identified experience database. The team includes
        writers and editors with a background in health communication. It does not include a physician, nurse
        practitioner, pharmacist or other licensed clinician who signs off on individual pages.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        That means the site can summarise what public guidance says. It cannot assess your medical history, your
        medicines, your pregnancy, your mental health or your comorbidities — and it does not try to.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">2. What “not reviewed by a clinician” means here</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        On this site the phrase means exactly what it says. A page has been written and edited against the cited
        sources, checked for consistency with those sources, and proofread — but no licensed clinician has read that
        specific page and confirmed it. Pages that carry a medical claim show this disclosure at the bottom.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        We do not use the words “medically reviewed”, “clinically reviewed”, “doctor-approved” or “medically verified”
        anywhere on this site, and we do not display reviewer names, credentials, headshots or review badges. If a
        clinician ever joins the review process, this page will say who they are, what they reviewed and when, before
        any page starts claiming review.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">3. The three kinds of page on this site</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700">
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold text-heading dark:text-slate-200">Page type</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold text-heading dark:text-slate-200">What it is</th>
              <th class="py-2 font-bold text-heading dark:text-slate-200">What it is not</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-slate-800">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-heading dark:text-slate-300">Evidence pages</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">Summaries of public guidance and systematic reviews: methods, medications, withdrawal, triggers, special situations.</td>
              <td class="py-3">A prescription, a dosing guide, or a recommendation for an individual.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-slate-800">
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-heading dark:text-slate-300">Question answers</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">Long-form answers to the questions people search for, each tied to the same source base.</td>
              <td class="py-3">A diagnosis, or a substitute for a consultation.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-heading dark:text-slate-300">Community reports</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-4">De-identified, structured accounts of one person's quit attempt, published only when they pass a quality gate.</td>
              <td class="py-3">Scientific evidence, a population claim, or a typical case.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">4. Where the evidence comes from</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        We work down a fixed source hierarchy. When sources disagree, the page says so rather than picking the more
        dramatic answer.
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading dark:text-slate-200">Clinical guidelines and public health bodies:</strong> WHO
          (including the 2024 tobacco cessation guideline), NICE NG209, USPSTF, CDC, NHS, NIH, FDA.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading dark:text-slate-200">Systematic reviews and trials:</strong> Cochrane reviews and
          the primary trials they summarise, recorded in our research register as R-001 to R-017.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading dark:text-slate-200">Peer-reviewed primary studies:</strong> used when no review
          covers the question, with design and limitations stated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading dark:text-slate-200">Community reports:</strong> used to describe what people
          report, never to establish what works.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        Research records store the title, authors, year, journal, DOI or PMID where one exists, population, method,
        main findings, limitations and a verification date. The register is published on the{' '}
        <a href="/research/" class="text-primary underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">research highlights page</a>{' '}
        and in the{' '}
        <a
          href="https://data.smokingcessationhub.com/"
          class="text-primary underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2"
          rel="noopener">data and research centre</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">5. How uncertainty is shown</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        Every evidence claim carries a strength label — Strong, Moderate, Limited, Mixed or Insufficient — and
        community material is labelled community report only. Where the evidence is thin, the page says it is thin.
        Where a widely repeated claim is not supported, the page says that too, and explains what the studies actually
        measured.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        We do not convert one person's outcome into a success rate, correlation into causation, or a surrogate endpoint
        into a promise about long-term health.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">6. What we will not publish</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Doses, titration schedules, injection technique, or instructions to obtain prescription medicines.</li>
        <li>Claims that a method cures nicotine dependence, guarantees abstinence, or works for everyone.</li>
        <li>Invented clinicians, reviewers, credentials, clinical certifications, studies, statistics, DOIs or PMIDs.</li>
        <li>Community posts copied verbatim, or translated and republished as our own writing.</li>
        <li>Testimonials framed as proof of effectiveness.</li>
        <li>Personalised advice for a named individual, including in response to emails.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">7. Dates, updates and AI assistance</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        Pages show the date they were last edited. That date reflects an editorial change, not a clinical review. We do
        not backdate pages, and we do not add review dates that did not happen.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        Drafting and maintenance are carried out with AI-assisted editorial tooling. Every published page is checked
        against its cited sources before it goes live, and the source list is visible on the page. AI assistance is
        never presented as clinical expertise, and no page is described as reviewed by a person who does not exist.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        Guidance changes. When WHO, NICE, USPSTF or the Cochrane Library publishes an update that affects a page, the
        page is revised and the edit date changes. Pages whose sources have been superseded are revised or withdrawn
        rather than left to age quietly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">8. Corrections</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        If a page misstates a source, overstates evidence, or contains a factual error, tell us through the{' '}
        <a href="/contact/" class="text-primary underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">contact page</a> and include
        the URL and the passage. Corrections that change meaning are made on the page and noted in the edit date.
        Corrections that are purely typographic are made without a note.
      </p>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        We will not remove a page because it is unflattering to a product or method. We will remove or rewrite a page
        that turns out to be wrong.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading mb-3">9. If you need clinical help</h2>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
        This site cannot provide it. For cessation medicines, pregnancy, mental health conditions, cardiovascular or
        respiratory disease, talk to a pharmacist, GP or specialist cessation service. If you are in immediate distress
        or having a medical emergency, contact your local emergency number.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources sources={pageSources} maintainer="SmokingCessationHub Editorial Team" />
</Layout>
